{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ARCHITECTURE RESEARCH — bounded live Pandoc boundary plus static corpus (2026-08-14; no ADR draft or implementation yet).\n\nCurrent constraint: accepted ADR 0095 states that every conversion assertion uses real pinned Pandoc and no test monkeypatches it. The shipped dependency is pypandoc-binary==1.15 / Pandoc 3.6.1. The committed legacy fixture pins darwin-arm64 SHA-256 94ebf1efbce3561379e8f25de3efe5aeabee64dc36dd8e8b9e96cf05b4195c52 and linux-x86_64 4715627586c5d9c732e8f5a6b6bb9e27c4216a76a7729e043b24374dedf8a1f0. Therefore full hot-path substitution requires an explicit ADR 0095 supersession; it cannot be treated as an implementation detail.\n\nCurrent cost and boundary map: a fresh same-host macOS three-worker run of test_wiki_render_corpus.py plus test_wiki_render_hardening.py passed 51 tests in 38.64s / real 38.80s (user 27.56s, sys 25.32s). Run 31798375024 attributed 149.03s setup to the shared pass-1 corpus and 35.29s to the prose fixed-point call; those two visible phases alone are a 184.32s critical-path lower bound, excluding the hardening chunks that each stay below 30s. The corpus tests assert cardinality/secrets, protected excerpts, exact tables/comments, deterministic settling, richness ratios, and a non-vacuous live dispatch. The hardening suite asserts all 884 prepared inputs and immutable expected outputs align, exact binary provenance, and product _convert bytes equal the landed golden bytes for every input. A superseding design must preserve these assertion classes by running segmentation/preservation/fixed-point logic against committed pre-rendered pass outputs in Verify, retain a small representative real _convert/Pandoc contract on both gating platforms, and move the complete real-Pandoc replay of every corpus unit and every settling pass to the existing weekly/manual external-integration workflow. Pin drift must fail fast and the existing deterministic generator remains the regeneration path.\n\nVerified upstream practice (source read at pinned current branch SHAs):\n- Pandoc 03a0a6484321: test/Tests/Writers/Jira.hs uses literal expected Jira writer outputs for compact construct cases.\n- nbconvert 78ed30837a60: tests/filters/test_pandoc.py and tests/utils/test_pandoc.py use only small real Pandoc probes (relative-path pair and empty/version/availability calls), not a repeated production-sized corpus.\n- pypandoc f57e9ab51049: tests/test_pypandoc.py uses small representative real conversions and explicitly says broader format coverage would test Pandoc rather than pypandoc.\n- Kubernetes client-go 3fcdd4c72588: dynamic/golden_test.go stores committed request/response fixtures and drives the client through httptest/fake transports rather than a real cluster; UPDATE_DYNAMIC_CLIENT_FIXTURES is the explicit regeneration switch.\n- Rust 059bf4a660dd: rustc-dev-guide UI tests store blessed .stdout/.stderr snapshots, require compact in-source diagnostic annotations as an independent anti-mistake oracle, and normalize platform noise.\nAll five repositories are active and unarchived; current stars were Pandoc 45,865, nbconvert 1,933, pypandoc 1,151, client-go 9,865, and Rust 115,504. No surveyed source documents rejecting bounded live probes plus static/golden routine assertions for reliability. The ticket-defined >=2/3 consensus threshold passes.\n\nResearch critique before DRAFT: (1) unverified assumption: exact post-refactor Verify cost remains an estimate until a RED/GREEN implementation run; current lower bound is 184.32s macOS CI and same-host removable wall is 38.80s. (2) dependency still to investigate during DRAFT: none for the architectural boundary; GitHub schedule and current generator/provenance route are already inspected. (3) unanswered: exact representative input set must be chosen by strata and mutation sensitivity during TDD, not in the ADR. (4) conflict: ADR 0095 is direct and must be marked Superseded by the new record in the same change. Per the architecture-decision lifecycle, DRAFT is gated on explicit team confirmation of this research summary."},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786711894881256001,"uuid":"8cc9bc07-311c-4f1d-b8cb-bbbf27f4e72a"}